Section 3: A Vote of No Confidence
What IP address did they forget to hide in the poster?
This was just on the image before.
Answer: 55.49.227.170

Is there any evidence of traffic from this IP address to our network? (yes/no)
This query should do the trick:
InboundNetworkEvents
| where src_ip == "55.49.227.170"
Answer: no

How many domains resolved to the IP 55.49.**.***?
This one uses PassiveDns.
PassiveDns
| where ip contains "55.49."
Answer: 2

What is the Valdoria related domain resolving to that IP?
Same query results: valdoriavotesgov.com

What is the legitimate domain for the Valdoria Elections Board?
Answer: valdoriavotes.gov

How many IP addresses did the fraudulent Valdoria government domain resolve to?
This query should look up that fraudulent odmain and resolve the IPs associated with it.
PassiveDns
| where domain == "valdoriavotesgov.com"
Answer: 3

Let’s check if there’s any browsing activity from these IPs to our network. Which table should we be looking at for records of that kind of activity again?
InboundNetworkEvents

How many requests do we see to our network from those IPs?
Given:
let ips = PassiveDns
| where domain == "valdoriavotesgov.com"
| distinct ip;
InboundNetworkEvents
| where src_ip  in (ips)
This will set a variable for unique IPs associated with the suspicious domain. Then, it will take those IPs and look for inbound (into our network) connections.
Answer: 26

